{"event_type":"review","id":"29fd2603d021d51298dd868e4ab36d1d65fcde36ee378c474c198c52fea07106","occurred_at":"2026-11-05T19:58:11Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/878c9ba36c8ef5f505f48e8bf5ec906d33c1e99f9ab3100b4f6d19c3747ca0e4","sha256":"878c9ba36c8ef5f505f48e8bf5ec906d33c1e99f9ab3100b4f6d19c3747ca0e4"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/4e9e238dee8754586d9326588fb06daf47f113ec78f81bc6f92a55041d5dd5c6","sha256":"4e9e238dee8754586d9326588fb06daf47f113ec78f81bc6f92a55041d5dd5c6"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/84ca08c5548755e82fd7cfb45849944a03a3c61d2efbc5188a92e5d1c6c9536d","sha256":"84ca08c5548755e82fd7cfb45849944a03a3c61d2efbc5188a92e5d1c6c9536d"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/a5eaffc40d4e915225525c022f0a2fd7072bb1560b0944ffe782aff341e20334","sha256":"a5eaffc40d4e915225525c022f0a2fd7072bb1560b0944ffe782aff341e20334"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/08303814a83d6eeb4f009a26552a8bcf226c8b90be7ff083ee35bc80889f85ec","sha256":"08303814a83d6eeb4f009a26552a8bcf226c8b90be7ff083ee35bc80889f85ec"}],"attempt_id":"de48788ede590655b75f070391c5525e1429f231e01d660c2ea37446bf0accdb:0:1","base":"df5273f48d3ac2a6cea57f5fd83487af90245301","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"3abaabbeb7a3249f5e3eb869713fc84dea0f0944","body":"**Wire `options.signal` to the `ssh` child in `sshQueueTransport`.**\n\n`refuseOnLifetime` throws on an aborted signal only when it runs. After that check, the transport does not read `options.signal`. In `src/ops/review`, `queueClient.ts` references `signal` only at lines 52 and 64. No code in the transport path kills the child or rejects when the caller aborts.\n\nA caller abort during a running `ssh` child does not stop that child. The child runs until it exits or the 45 s timer fires. The abort reason is not propagated. An abort during `report` can therefore be delayed until the in-flight request ends, up to 45 s.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n+      const onAbort = () => {\n+        child.kill('SIGKILL');\n+        reject(options?.signal?.reason ?? new Error('queue delivery unknown: aborted'));\n+      };\n+      options?.signal?.addEventListener('abort', onAbort, { once: true });\n       const timer = setTimeout(\n```\n\nRemove the listener wherever the timer is cleared, using `options?.signal?.removeEventListener('abort', onAbort)`. This keeps a finished child from being killed later.\n</details>","id":"f374031b7cd997f7cbcc2a87bd8498be04432c46ff7e7d05fcd72d4e0d137a45","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/queueClient.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Wire `options.signal` to the `ssh` child in `sshQueueTransport`."}],"head":"a15764dc834d2c72434bad6b777f77ed54d71be3","head_tree":"a044c2d307ae73d8952cea17b0d4c6811610cdec","input_scope":[{"blob":"2a04639d2c91885cbc6281cb8c6a404fa87839db","intervals":[[1,1],[15,15],[24,24],[38,38],[44,44],[46,50],[52,62],[72,84],[86,90],[95,97],[107,108],[112,113],[122,126],[132,142],[145,145],[161,173],[179,180],[187,191],[195,197],[211,214],[263,269],[275,278],[291,295],[315,315],[327,338],[341,363],[385,399],[463,471],[474,477],[549,550],[552,553],[555,559],[567,567],[615,615],[624,635],[647,675],[684,684],[687,698],[708,710],[712,712],[716,716],[722,725],[730,737],[740,747],[758,761],[763,807],[809,853],[855,855],[857,857],[860,889],[891,894],[897,899],[901,910],[912,912],[917,923],[925,925],[930,998],[1000,1013],[1015,1316],[1319,1320],[1325,1333],[1335,1408],[1410,1425],[1427,1439],[1442,1449],[1451,1492],[1494,1496],[1498,1501],[1503,1702],[1704,1714],[1716,2019],[2024,2062],[2064,2070],[2074,2083],[2085,2109],[2111,2142],[2144,2204],[2206,2241],[2243,2246],[2249,2251],[2